"EchoStar Changing Stock Ticker SATS to ECHO, Marking the Company's Next Era on Earth and in Space | EchoStar Corporation (https://echostar.gcs-web.com/news-releases/news-release-details/echostar-changing-stocker-ticker-sats-echo-marking-companys-next)\nciteturn14search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Crawled: yesterday; \n\nEchoStar Changing Stock Ticker SATS to ECHO, Marking the Company's Next Era on Earth and in Space\n\nJune 22, 2026\n\n### EchoStar Corporation is officially changing its Nasdaq stock ticker symbol from \"SATS\" to \"ECHO\" Effective June 24, 2026\n\nKey Takeaways\n\n  * Ticker Change: EchoStar Corporation is changing its Nasdaq stock ticker symbol from \"SATS\" to \"ECHO\"\n  * Effective Date: The new ticker will begin trading on June 24, 2026\n  * Shareholder Impact: No action is required from current shareholders; ticker conversions will happen automatically\n  * Rationale: The stock ticker transition highlights EchoStar's expansion beyond traditional satellite services into a global connectivity brand\n\nENGLEWOOD, Colo., June 22, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- EchoStar Corporation, the parent company of DISH Network, Boost Mobile, Sling TV, and Hughes Network Systems, today announced that it will change its Nasdaq stock ticker symbol from \"SATS\" to \"ECHO\" to better represent the company's expanding lines of business.\n\nEchoStar’s common stock will begin trading under the new ticker symbol “ECHO” on the Nasdaq effective June 24, 2026. The CUSIP number for the Company’s common stock is not affected by the stock symbol change.\n\n\"We have spent decades building brands that challenge the status quo and deliver real value to customers,\" said Charlie Ergen, Founder, CEO, and Chairman of the Board, EchoStar Corporation. \"Changing our stock ticker to ‘ECHO’ represents our growth from a pure-play satellite company to a global corporate leader with a diverse set of connectivity assets.”\n\nEchoStar’s Legacy\nEchoStar Communications Corporation was founded in 1980 selling C-band satellite dish systems to rural Americans. In 1995, after years of building a successful business, EchoStar opted to take its future to space, launching its first direct broadcast satellite to provide TV service nationwide. With this launch, DISH Network was born, delivering one industry-shaking innovation after another. In 2008, in recognition of this massive growth, the original company was officially renamed DISH Network and continued as a publicly traded company under the symbol \"DISH.\" Concurrently, the critical satellite infrastructure and technology assets were separated into a new, independent publicly traded company named EchoStar Corporation, trading under the symbol \"SATS.\"\n\nOperating under its own mandate to connect the world, EchoStar expanded its global footprint by acquiring Hughes Network Systems in June 2011 and launching a series of advanced satellites to provide connectivity to enterprise, government, and consumer markets across the globe. In 2020, DISH completed its acquisition of Boost Mobile, accelerating the company’s growth into consumer wireless.\n\nAfter years of operating as separate companies, EchoStar and DISH merged in December 2023, trading under a single stock ticker. Today’s announcement of EchoStar’s new ticker “ECHO” honors the company's original namesake—NASA’s pioneering Project Echo, the first communications satellite project—and reflects the future of EchoStar on earth, in space, and beyond. \n\nAdditional Details for Shareholders\nThis transition to a new ticker symbol will have no impact on the corporation's legal name, its capital structure, or the established rights of its securityholders.\n\nAll existing stock certificates will stay valid and do not require exchange. Shares maintained in book-entry form or via financial institutions and brokers will be updated to show the new ticker symbol automatically.\n\nAbout EchoStar Corporation\nEchoStar Corporation is a premier provider of technology, networking services, television entertainment and connectivity, offering consumer, enterprise, operator and government solutions worldwide under its EchoStar®, Boost Mobile®, Sling TV, DISH TV, Hughes®, HughesNet®, HughesON™, and JUPITER™ brands. In Europe, EchoStar operates under its EchoStar Mobile Limited subsidiary and in Australia, the company operates as EchoStar Global Australia. For more information, visit www.echostar.com and follow EchoStar on X (Twitter) and LinkedIn.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEverpure to Change Ticker Symbol to “P” | Everpure (https://www.everpuredata.com/company/newsroom/press-releases/everpure-to-change-ticker-symbol.html)\nciteturn14search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; \n\nPress Release\n\n# Everpure to Change Ticker Symbol to “P”\n\nImage: Everpure to Change Ticker Symbol\n\nSanta Clara, CA – April 7, 2026 — Everpure (NYSE: PSTG), the company revolutionizing storage and data management, today announced it will change its stock ticker symbol from “PSTG” to “P” on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE). Trading under the new ticker symbol is expected to begin on Friday, April 17, 2026.\n\nThe new ticker symbol aligns to the company’s recent rebrand to Everpure announced on February 23, 2026. The single-letter ticker symbol “P” honors the “Pure” at the heart of Everpure and the company’s strategy to expand beyond storage as it simplifies how organizations manage and unleash the power of their data in the AI era.\n\nThere is no action required by the company’s shareholders in connection with the ticker symbol change. The company’s common stock will continue to be listed on the NYSE, and its CUSIP number will remain unchanged.\n\n#### About Everpure\n\nEverpure (NYSE: PSTG) allows organizations to take control of their data with an industry-leading, ever-evolving storage and data management platform. We help companies unleash the power of their data by ensuring it is accessible, intelligent, and ready to perform in the AI era. We make data management effortless while simultaneously scaling performance and significantly reducing energy consumption. With one of the highest Net Promoter Scores for over a decade, Everpure is the choice of the world’s most innovative organizations. For more information, visit www.Everpuredata.com.\n\nPress Contact\n\nImage\n\nTricia Stream\n\nGlobal Communications, Everpure\n\npr@purestorage.com pr@purestorage.com--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEchoStar Changing Stock Ticker SATS to ECHO, Marking the Company's Next Era on Earth and in Space (https://ir.echostar.com/node/33601/pdf)\nciteturn14search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; EchoStar Corporation is officially changing its Nasdaq stock ticker symbol from \"SATS\" to \"ECHO\" Effective June 24, 2026 ... ENGLEWOOD, Colo., June 22, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- EchoStar Corporation, the parent company of DISH Network, Boost Mobile, Sling TV, and Hughes Network Systems, today announced that it will change its Nasdaq stock ticker symbol from \"SATS\" to \"ECHO\" to better represent the company's expanding lines of business.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMIAX Exchange Group - Options Markets - Corporate Action Alert: EchoStar Corporation (SATS) Trading Symbol Change | MIAX (https://www.miaxglobal.com/alert/2026/06/23/miax-exchange-group-options-markets-corporate-action-alert-echostar)\nciteturn14search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Crawled: 4 weeks ago; \n\n# U.S. Options\n\nMIAX Pearl Options Alerts\n\nFind more information on our U.S. options exchanges.\n\nListing Alert, Trading Alert, Regulatory Alert\n\nMIAX Pearl\n\nJune 23, 2026 | 03:52 PM\n\n###### MIAX Exchange Group - Options Markets - Corporate Action Alert: EchoStar Corporation (SATS) Trading Symbol Change\n\nEchoStar Corporation (SATS) will change its trading symbol to (ECHO) effective Wednesday, June 24, 2026. \nAll GTC orders resting on the MIAX order books in SATS will be canceled at the close of business on Tuesday, June 23, 2026.\nNOTE: ECHO options will trade on Cloud 5 on the MIAX Options Exchange, Cloud 3 on the MIAX Pearl Options Exchange and MIAX Emerald Options Exchange and Cloud 2 on the MIAX Sapphire Options Exchange.\nAdditional details about the EchoStar Corporation (SATS) symbol change are provided in the attached OCC Memo.\nPlease contact MIAX Listings with any questions at Listings@miaxglobal.com or (609) 897-7308.\n\n  * SATS Symbol Change 59221--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPost From: Symbol P missing data - Support Board - Sierra Chart (https://www.sierrachart.com/SupportBoard.php?PostID=441499)\nciteturn14search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; \n\n#### Home >> Support Board\n\n# Support Board\n\nDate/Time: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:34:53 +0000\n\n* * *\n\nHow to Post a Message for Support\n\n* * *\n\n## Post From: Symbol P missing data\n\n[2026-04-27 19:09:54] Link To Thread - Link To Post [Go To First Post]\nJohn - SC Support - Posts: 48062\nThey changed their ticker symbol on April 17, 2026. Refer to the following:\nhttps://www.purestorage.com/company/newsroom/press-releases/everpure-to-change-ticker-symbol.html\nYou would have to opan a chart for PSTG to see the data prior to April 17, 2026.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEquity Residential and AvalonBay Communities Announce Shareholder Approvals for Merger to Create Vivmark Residential | Equity Residential (https://investors.equityapartments.com/news-events/press-releases-news/news-details/2026/Equity-Residential-and-AvalonBay-Communities-Announce-Shareholder-Approvals-for-Merger-to-Create-Vivmark-Residential/default.aspx)\nciteturn14search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; \n\n## Press Release\n\n## Equity Residential and AvalonBay Communities Announce Shareholder Approvals for Merger to Create Vivmark Residential\n\nCompany Release - 8/12/2026\n\nMerger expected to close on August 17, 2026\n\nARLINGTON, Va. & CHICAGO--(BUSINESS WIRE)-- AvalonBay Communities, Inc. (“AvalonBay”) (NYSE: AVB) and Equity Residential (NYSE: EQR) today announced that at their respective special meetings, AvalonBay stockholders and Equity Residential shareholders overwhelmingly approved all of the proposals necessary to close the pending merger of equals between AvalonBay and Equity Residential (the “merger”). More than 99% of the votes cast at the AvalonBay special meeting voted to approve the merger, which represented approximately 90% of the outstanding shares of AvalonBay common stock, as of the record date, and more than 99% of the votes cast at Equity Residential’s special meeting voted to approve the issuance of Equity Residential common shares to AvalonBay stockholders as consideration in the merger, which represented approximately 90% of the outstanding Equity Residential common shares, as of the record date.\n\nThe final voting results on the proposals voted on at the special meetings will be set forth on Form 8-Ks to be filed by each company with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission.\n\nThe merger is expected to close on Monday, August 17, 2026, subject to the satisfaction or waiver of customary closing conditions. If the merger is completed, each share of AvalonBay common stock outstanding immediately prior to the merger will convert into the right to receive 2.793 Equity Residential common shares.\n\nFollowing the completion of the merger, the combined company will be renamed “Vivmark Residential,” with its common shares expected to trade on the New York Stock Exchange under the ticker symbol “VMRK” beginning at the open of trading on August 18, 2026.\n\nAbout AvalonBay Communities, Inc.\nAvalonBay Communities, Inc., a member of the S&P 500, is an equity REIT that develops, redevelops, acquires and manages apartment communities in leading metropolitan areas in Boston, Massachusetts, the New York/New Jersey Metro area, the Mid-Atlantic, Seattle, Washington, and Northern and Southern California, as well as in the Company's expansion regions of Raleigh-Durham and Charlotte, North Carolina, Southeast Florida, Dallas and Austin, Texas, and Denver, Colorado. As of June 30, 2026, the Company owned or held a direct or indirect ownership interest in 322 apartment communities containing 99,072 apartment homes in 11 states and the District of Columbia, of which 27 communities were under development and one community was under redevelopment. More information may be found on the Company’s website at https://www.avalonbay.com.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEquity Residential and AvalonBay Communities Announce Shareholder Approvals for Merger to Create Vivmark Residential (https://investors.avalonbay.com/_assets/_5b905ab7bc6a6fabe33b94e085cd3dde/avalonbay/news/2026-08-12_Equity_Residential_and_AvalonBay_Communities_445.pdf)\nciteturn14search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; More than 99% of the votes cast at the AvalonBay special meeting voted to approve the merger, which represented approximately 90% of the outstanding shares of AvalonBay common stock, as of the record date, and more than 99% of the votes cast at Equity Residential’s special meeting voted to approve the issuance of Equity Residential common shares to AvalonBay stockholders as consideration in the merger, which represented approximately 90% of the outstanding Equity Residential common shares, as of the record date. ... Following the completion of the merger, the combined company will be renamed “Vivmark Residential,” with its common shares expected to trade on the New York Stock Exchange under the ticker symbol “VMRK” beginning at the open of trading on August 18, 2026.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEchoStar Swaps SATS Ticker for ECHO to Emphasize Business Shift - Via Satellite (https://www.satellitetoday.com/finance/2026/06/22/echostar-swaps-sats-ticker-for-echo-to-emphasize-business-shift/)\nciteturn14search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Crawled: last month; \n\n# EchoStar Swaps SATS Ticker for ECHO to Emphasize Business Shift\n\nBy Image: Photo of Rachel Jewett Rachel Jewett\n\nMonday, June 22, 2026\n\nImage EchoStar's headquarters in Englewood, Colorado. Photo: EchoStar\n\nEchoStar is changing its stock ticker from “SATS” to “ECHO” to emphasize the company’s shift into a global connectivity business. \n\nEchoStar announced the move on June 22. Starting June 24, EchoStar’s stock will trade under the ticker symbol “ECHO.” EchoStar said it’s a nod to NASA’s Project Echo, the first communications satellite project, the original inspiration behind the company’s name. \n\n“Changing our stock ticker to ‘ECHO’ represents our growth from a pure-play satellite company to a global corporate leader with a diverse set of connectivity assets,” EchoStar founder, CEO, and Chairman Charlie Ergen said. \n\nEchoStar is at an interesting juncture as it transitions to an “asset-light growth company” with spectrum sales to SpaceX and AT&T. The FCC formally approved the SpaceX transaction in May. \n\nThe SpaceX transaction is set to occur in two steps detailed in EchoStar’s recent 10-K filing, with the spectrum transfer closing expected to occur in the first half of 2026 and the spectrum acquisition closing is expected to occur on or about November 30, 2027.\n\nEarlier this year, EchoStar CEO Hamid Akhavan said the company is “in the midst of a large-scale positive transformation arising from its vision, long horizon of strategic bets and decades of diligent execution,” but Echostar hasn’t provided more of an update on that future direction yet. \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPure Storage Is Now Everpure: What the Rebrand Means for Buyers (https://enterprisetechie.com/pure-storage-everpure-rebrand/)\nciteturn14search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Crawled: today; \n\n## What changed\n\nThe mechanics were quick and deliberately boring. Under Delaware law, a corporate name change requires no stockholder vote, so the amendment was filed on February 20 and the new name became effective the following Monday. Here is the timeline as it actually happened.\n\n | Date  | What happened\n--- | --- | ---\nFiling  | Feb 20, 2026  | Certificate of amendment filed with the Delaware Secretary of State\nName change  | Feb 23, 2026  | Pure Storage, Inc. becomes Everpure, Inc.; rebrand announced publicly\n1touch deal  | Same week  | Intent to acquire data-intelligence vendor 1touch; terms undisclosed. The deal was completed in May 2026\nEarnings  | Same week  | Q4 FY26 revenue of ~$1.06B — the company’s first billion-dollar quarter, up ~20% year over year\nTrading  | Mar 5, 2026  | Shares begin trading under the Everpure name on the NYSE, initially still as PSTG\nTicker  | Apr 17, 2026  | NYSE ticker symbol changes from PSTG to P\n\nWhat did not change matters just as much. FlashArray, FlashBlade, Portworx, and the Evergreen subscription programs keep their names as of mid-2026. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\npstg-20260223 (https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1474432/000147443226000011/pstg-20260223.htm)\nciteturn14search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Crawled: 8 months ago; \n\nIn connection with the Name Change, the Company’s Board of Directors also approved amended and restated bylaws, effective as of February 23, 2026, to reflect the Name Change (the \"Amended and Restated Bylaws\").\n\nFollowing the Name Change, the Company's shares of Class A common stock will continue to trade under the ticker symbol \"PSTG\" on the New York Stock Exchange.\n\nCopies of the Certificate of Amendment and the Amended and Restated Bylaws are filed as Exhibit 3.1 and Exhibit 3.2, respectively, with this Current Report on Form 8-K and are incorporated herein by reference. The only change to the Company’s prior amended and restated certificate of incorporation and prior amended and restated bylaws is the change of the Company’s corporate name from \"Pure Storage, Inc.\" to \"Everpure, Inc.\" in each document.\n\nItem 9.01 Financial Statements and Exhibits.\n\n(d) Exhibits.\n\nThe following exhibits are furnished herewith:\n |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | \nExhibit No.  |  | Description\n3.1  |  | Certificate of Amendment to the Amended and Restated Certificate of Incorporation\n3.2  |  | Amended and Restated Bylaws\n104  |  | Cover Page Interactive Data File (formatted as inline XBRL)\n\nSIGNATURES\n\nPursuant to the requirements of the Securities and Exchange Act of 1934, the Registrant has duly caused this report to be signed on its behalf by the undersigned thereunto duly authorized.\n\n \n |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | \n | Pure Storage, Inc.\n | (Registrant)\n   |    |  |  | \nDate:  |  | February 23, 2026  | By:  |    | /s/ Nicole Armstrong\n |  |  |    |    | Nicole Armstrong\n |  |  |    |    | Chief Administrative and Legal Officer--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVivmark Residential Launches as One of the Country's Leading Real Estate Companies :: Vivmark Residential (VMRK) (https://investors.vivmarkresidential.com/news-events/press-releases/detail/113/vivmark-residential-launches-as-one-of-the-countrys-leading-real-estate-companies)\nciteturn14search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: today; \n\nDividend\n\nVivmark Residential expects to deliver a current yield to investors through the payment of an initial expected annualized dividend of $2.81 per share.\n\nTransaction Details\n\nVivmark Residential is expected to trade on the NYSE under the ticker symbol VMRK beginning at the opening of trading on August 18, 2026.\n\nPursuant to the terms of the merger agreement between the parties, each share of AvalonBay common stock outstanding immediately prior to the merger converted into the right to receive 2.793 shares of the combined company. Following closing, former AvalonBay stockholders will own approximately 51% and Equity Residential shareholders will own approximately 49% of the combined company on a fully diluted basis. The transaction is expected to qualify as a tax-free reorganization for U.S. federal income tax purposes.\n\nCommitment to Affordable Housing\n\nVivmark Residential is committed to expanding access to affordable housing across the markets it serves. As part of this commitment, Vivmark Residential is deepening its partnership with True Ground Housing Partners, committing $1.5 million to expand resident services across True Ground's portfolio in the greater Washington, DC metro region.\n\nVivmark Residential also intends to establish an affordable housing bridge loan facility to provide predevelopment capital to nonprofit developers working to create and preserve affordable homes. Further details will be announced in the coming months.\n\nThese initiatives build on the affordable and mixed-income housing presence already embedded across 30% of Vivmark Residential's communities, representing approximately 7,200 affordable apartment homes. They also align with Vivmark’s broader development program, where approximately 50% of projects include affordable and mixed-income components.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSATS / ECHO — EchoStar Corporation - Deep Dives Hub (https://tomstocks-ai.github.io/deep-dives-hub/deep-dives/SATS/)\nciteturn14search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; \n\n# SATS / ECHO — EchoStar Corporation¶\n\nReport Date: August 4, 2026\nCurrent Price: $84.09 (August 3, 2026 close, VERIFIED)\nExchange: NASDAQ — ticker changed from SATS to ECHO effective June 24, 2026 (CUSIP, legal name and share rights unchanged)\nMarket Cap: ~$24.4 billion\nSector: Technology · Satellite Communications / Telecom\nAnalyst Rating: SPEC. BUY\n\n> Ticker note: This deep dive is filed under the legacy symbol SATS. EchoStar Corporation now trades on Nasdaq as ECHO (effective June 24, 2026). The company, CUSIP and capital structure are unchanged — only the trading symbol changed. Live quotes and the chart above use ECHO.\n\n## Executive Summary¶\n\nEchoStar has now executed the bulk of the transformation that defined the bull thesis a year ago. On June 30, 2026 the company deconsolidated its Pay-TV segment (DISH TV plus Sling) and substantially all of its \"Other\" segment, booking a $9.7 billion gain that pushed Q2 FY2026 net income to $8.5 billion (versus a $306 million loss a year earlier). --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEquity Residential and AvalonBay Communities Announce Shareholder Approvals for Merger to Create Vivmark Residential :: Vivmark Residential (VMRK) (https://investors.vivmarkresidential.com/news-events/press-releases/detail/112/equity-residential-and-avalonbay-communities-announce-shareholder-approvals-for-merger-to-create-vivmark-residential)\nciteturn14search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: today; \nView source version on businesswire.com: https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260812892568/en/\n\nSource: Equity Residential\n\nReleased August 12, 2026--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPure Storage Inc. (PSTG) | Stock Price History & Returns | 2015 - 2026 (https://devyara.com/en-us/nyse/pstg/price-history/)\nciteturn14search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; \nApr 22, 2026  | $69.36  | +0.27%  | $70.19  | $71.16  | $68.81  | 3.0M\nApr 21, 2026  | $69.17  | +1.72%  | $68.15  | $70.26  | $67.65  | 2.4M\nApr 20, 2026  | $68.00  | +1.54%  | $66.87  | $68.54  | $66.24  | 2.2M\nApr 17, 2026  | $66.97  | -1.22%  | $68.00  | $69.10  | $66.97  | 2.0M\nApr 16, 2026  | $67.80  | +4.48%  | $65.44  | $67.83  | $64.54  | 2.8M\nApr 15, 2026  | $64.89  | +1.39%  | $64.35  | $65.25  | $63.92  | 2.3M\nApr 14, 2026  | $64.00  | +1.19%  | $64.60  | $64.67  | $62.75  | 2.6M\nApr 13, 2026  | $63.25  | +3.79%  | $60.41  | $63.30  | $60.41  | 2.6M\nApr 10, 2026  | $60.94  | +1.25%  | $61.02  | $61.45  | $60.20  | 2.2M\nApr 9, 2026  | $60.19  | -3.31%  | $62.46  | $63.15  | $59.40  | 2.4M\nApr 8, 2026  | $62.25  | +0.58%  | $65.28  | $65.95  | $61.82  | 5.4M\nApr 7, 2026  | $61.89  | +1.18%  | $60.62  | $62.31  | $60.31  | 1.8M\nApr 6, 2026  | $61.17  | -2.10%  | $62.56  | $63.80  | $61.05  | 1.8M\nApr 2, 2026  | $62.48  | +2.31%  | $59.00  | $62.58  | $58.91  | 1.9M\nApr 1, 2026  | $61.07  | +3.44%  | $60.76  | $62.45  | $60.00  | 2.6M\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEverything you need to know about Pure Storage (https://www.itpro.com/hardware/storage/everything-you-need-to-know-about-pure-storage)\nciteturn14news33 [wordlim: 100] Published: last year; With a market cap fluctuating between $16 and $22 billion in 2025, and annual revenue reaching $3.2 billion in the 2025, an impressive increase from $2.8 billion the previous year Pure Storage exemplifies the resilience and potential of modern tech companies. ... The annual Pure//Accelerate conference, launched in 2016, became a signature event to showcase its latest advancements, including its focus on AI and cloud integration. ... The company now trades on the New York Stock Exchange under the ticker PSTG.\nEverything you need to know about Pure Storage\nDate: Fri Oct 31 18:26:18 2025 UTC\n\nOnce a disruptive startup in a venture capital conference room, Pure Storage has grown into a global leader in data storage technology. Founded with the ambitious goal of transforming enterprise storage, the company introduced all-flash arrays that challenged conventional norms in the industry. Its pioneering efforts laid the foundation for a new era in data management, one where speed, scalability, and reliability are paramount. This early focus on innovation and performance has propelled Pure Storage into an indispensable role within the tech infrastructure of countless industries.\nOver the years, the company's solutions have evolved to address complex demands across various sectors. Universities rely on their technology to support breakthroughs in research, while financial institutions depend on Pure Storage for robust systems that ensure secure and seamless transactions. Other prominent users include Sirius XM, which leverages the company's data platform to deliver uninterrupted streaming to millions of subscribers. From its humble beginnings to its current status as an industry leader, the company's story is a testament to the power of vision and dedication in reshaping the technological landscape.\nHere is a broad overview of the path the company has taken to become one of the most prominent names in storage, with a market cap of $21.75 billion to match.\nFounded\n2009 under the temporary name 'Os76', unveiled as Pure Storage in 2011\nCurrent CEO\nCharles Giancarlo\nHQ\nSanta Clara, California\nAnnual revenue\n$3.2 billion for fiscal year 2025, showing growth from $2.8 billion in 2024\n\nA quick history of Pure Storage\n\nPure Storage was founded with venture capital funding from Sutter Hill and an ambitious goal: to define the \"Modern Data Experience.\" Its introduction of flash storage solutions, such as FlashArray and FlashBlade, revolutionized enterprise environments, particularly data centers. By addressing the inefficiencies of traditional hard disk drives (HDDs) with modern solid-state drives (SSDs), Pure Storage established itself as a pioneer in data storage innovation.\nThe company entered the market at a time when businesses were transitioning to more advanced storage technologies but lacked the infrastructure to support significant change. John 'Coz' Colgrove, a founding engineer from Veritas, and John Hayes, a former Yahoo CTO, identified this technological gap, termed the \"Flash Chasm,\" and built solutions to bridge it. Their vision enabled Pure Storage to become a significant player in the enterprise storage market.\nPure Storage went public in 2015, further cementing its influence in the industry. That same year, the company settled a patent dispute with EMC for $30 million, which demonstrated its willingness to protect its intellectual property and market position.\nThe annual Pure//Accelerate conference, launched in 2016, became a signature event to showcase its latest advancements, including its focus on AI and cloud integration. These conferences continue to highlight Pure's strategy to align with emerging technological trends.\nAs the importance of generative AI has grown, Pure Storage has positioned itself as a critical infrastructure provider for these demanding workloads. Its flash storage systems are designed to scale to the petabyte levels required for AI applications, supporting businesses in their digital transformation journeys. CEO Charles Giancarlo has frequently emphasized how Pure's solutions cater to the unique storage needs of AI, which demand speed, scalability, and sustainability.\nTo reinforce this position, the company has made strategic investments in AI infrastructure, such as its partnership with CoreWeave, an AI cloud provider. By combining cutting-edge technology with a focus on sustainability, Pure Storage continues to meet the evolving needs of enterprises while maintaining its leadership in the competitive storage market.\n\nWhat does Pure Storage sell?\n\nPure Storage provides a wide range of flash storage solutions designed for data centres, complemented by software and platform tools that optimize data storage and usage. Its product lineup includes the FlashArray series, ideal for block storage, and FlashBlade, which caters to file and object data.\nThe company has placed significant emphasis on delivering its offerings as a service. Customers can choose cloud storage options tailored to private cloud, public cloud, and hybrid cloud. environments, including integration with  AWS and Azure. A standout offering, the Evergreen subscription model, ensures seamless upgrades to both hardware and software, fostering sustainability and prolonged hardware lifespans. This service model competes with the likes of HPE GreenLake and Dell Apex.\nRecent developments have introduced features aimed at making storage systems more intelligent and automated. During its annual conference, the company unveiled Evergreen//One for AI, a pioneering storage-as-a-service product for AI applications, and an AI-driven assistant for storage management that leverages insights from customer systems to streamline operations.\nPure Storage works at the enterprise level across the private and public sectors, having worked with ScotGov to overhaul its storage approach and embrace containers, and with Mississippi's tax authority to support critical apps.\nBeyond physical arrays, Pure Storage offers storage and disaster recovery as a service products, data security solutions, AI-focused offerings, and its 'Storage-as-Code' options. Its tagline is \"uncomplicate data storage, forever\".\nIts consumption-based storage subscription service Evergreen competes with the likes of HPE GreenLake and Dell Apex.\n\nPure Storage's mergers and acquisitions\n\nBefore its initial public offering in 2015, Pure Storage had already secured substantial funding, including one of the largest investment rounds in its sector at the time. The company now trades on the New York Stock Exchange under the ticker PSTG.\nOver the years, Pure Storage has strategically acquired several companies to strengthen its portfolio. These include:\n\nDoing Business with Pure Storage\n\nBased in Silicon Valley, Pure Storage serves prominent clients such as Ford, Meta, JP Morgan Chase, and NASA. Its operations extend globally, with offices across Europe, Latin America, and the Asia-Pacific regions.\nIn 2025, the company revamped its partner program to enhance profitability and provide partners with tools to drive customer adoption of its platforms, particularly for artificial intelligence and cyber resilience. The updated program includes an automated system for managing service agreements and new incentives to encourage the replacement of outdated disk storage systems.\n[Image 0: The economics of penetration testing for web application security]\nGet the most value from your security solution\nFrom an internal policy perspective, Pure Storage remains committed to its goal of achieving net-zero greenhouse gas emissions for its direct operations by 2040. A key selling point for the company is the sustainability of its products; it claims its all-flash solutions can significantly reduce data center energy consumption by up to 85% compared to competitor systems.\nThe company's 2024 ESG report highlights its commitment to helping customers lessen their environmental impact through reduced energy and space usage, as well as minimizing e-waste. Pure Storage plans to submit its science-based emissions reduction targets for approval in July 2024.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPure Storage: Fiscal Q2 Earnings Snapshot (https://apnews.com/article/8aa48672b267121040087cea2321d822)\nciteturn14news37 [wordlim: 100] Published: 3.2 years ago; Pure Storage: Fiscal Q2 Earnings Snapshot ... Access a  Zacks stock report on PSTG  at https://www.zacks.com/ap/PSTG\nPure Storage: Fiscal Q2 Earnings Snapshot\nDate: Wed Aug 30 20:16:57 2023 UTC\nLocation: Santa Clara, California, United States\n\nSANTA CLARA, Calif. (AP) - SANTA CLARA, Calif. (AP) - Pure Storage Inc. (PSTG) on Wednesday reported a loss of $7.1 million in its fiscal second quarter.\nOn a per-share basis, the Santa Clara, California-based company said it had a loss of 2 cents. Earnings, adjusted for stock option expense and non-recurring costs, were 34 cents per share.\nThe results exceeded Wall Street expectations. The average estimate of 11 analysts surveyed by Zacks Investment Research was for earnings of 28 cents per share.\nThe data storage company posted revenue of $688.7 million in the period, also beating Street forecasts. Ten analysts surveyed by Zacks expected $681.3 million.\nFor the current quarter ending in October, Pure Storage said it expects revenue in the range of $760 million.\n_____\nThis story was generated by  Automated Insights  (http://automatedinsights.com/ap) using data from Zacks Investment Research. Access a  Zacks stock report on PSTG  at https://www.zacks.com/ap/PSTG\n"
